  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Durable Solutions for Crisis Affected Populations in North-East Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to promote durable solutions for crisis affected populations in North-East Nigeria through the development of settlements and the provision of integrated services in order to enable the sustainable integration of displaced households within local communities. The project presents a multi-sectoral and multilevel approach which includes shelter &amp; non-food items, water, sanitation and hygiene, and protection. These integrated services are to be provided to approximately 1,500 returned internally displaced persons. In addition to this, durable solutions-oriented interventions in support of displaced populations are implemented alongside multi-stakeholder consultations, including with the Government of Nigeria and crisis affected populations, for the development of a viable durable solutions- strategy to address protracted displacement in the region. IOM is also working towards durable solutions specifically supporting persons with disabilities (PWDs), by facilitating identification of PWDs, improving their access to services, and making referrals to specialists working in Borno or Adamawa State of Nigeria. This pilot project seeks to provide an evidence-based model in addressing protracted displacement in North-East Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
